{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall dwell near me.</b> Goshen was near to Egypt, and Joseph knew his father — that he would not want to dwell in the city of Egypt, where the seat of the kingdom was, and therefore he sent to him to settle him in the land of Goshen. And as for what it says, <b>and there will I nourish you, lest you come to poverty,</b> it means: if you remain in the land of Canaan you will come to poverty, and I am unable to nourish you there, lest the people of the land suspect me that I am sending grain there to sell in order to make there stores of silver and hidden treasures, and that my wish is to return to the land of my birth; but when you all come to Goshen, near to Egypt, everyone will know that my father and my brothers have come to me, and then the king will grant me permission. Thus explained the Ramban."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:19.694044019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}